<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan Vicente Gómez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1857">1857</a>–<a href="/years/1935">1935</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan Vicente Gómez was a soldier from the Andes who seized power in Venezuela in 1908 and ruled as dictator until his death in 1935. His regime crushed opposition, centralised the state and built a professional army. Oil was discovered under his rule, and through concessions to foreign companies Venezuela became one of the world's leading oil exporters.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juan-vicente-gomez.jpg" alt="Juan Vicente Gómez" width="320" height="463" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author, Restored version by Wilfredor · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:G%C3%B3mez,_1928_restored.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
